    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0146" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v19p2/pg115"/>

                <head>36. Memorandum From President Nixon to
                    the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs (Kissinger)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d36-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1969-11-24">November 24, 1969</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>As you will note in my final talk with Sato<anchor n="2" xml:id="d36-f2"/> he hedged on the use of the
                    word comprehensive. I want you to read the transcript very carefully and then
                    follow up. We have to drive a hard bargain at Geneva and I think Sato expects us to do so.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
